&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mozilla/contract-staff-software-engineer-bug-burndown-24999","tags":["Firefox"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792659320},{"slug":"contract-sr-data-analyst-sqltelemetrybrowser-engine-467983","company_name":"mozilla","title":"Contract Sr Data Analyst (SQL,Telemetry,Browser Engine)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The Gecko platform is the core engine of our product experience. To maintain competitiveness and user satisfaction, we must move beyond surface-level metrics to understand the deep correlations between engine performance and real-world user behavior. We currently face challenges with data quality, such as bot contamination in nightly telemetry, which obscures our understanding of true performance trends. A dedicated analyst is required to bridge the gap between engineering telemetry and actionable product strategy, ensuring that leadership has high-fidelity data to prioritize performance guardrails and technical budgets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Deliverables&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automated Dashboards:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Create and maintain high-level overview dashboards that translate complex performance data into consumable formats for Product Managers and leadership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Telemetry Gap Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Audit the Gecko codebase to identify missing collection points or &quot;probes&quot; necessary for a complete understanding of the product experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Sanitization Frameworks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Develop methodologies and tools to identify and filter data inconsistencies, specifically focusing on isolating bot traffic and hardware-specific noise from telemetry streams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioral Inference Reports:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Deliver deep-dive analyses correlating technical performance shifts (e.g., LCP, eTLD+1) with user-facing pain points and engagement trends.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope, Skills, and Effort Estimate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The analyst will focus exclusively on Gecko engine telemetry across multiple platforms (Desktop and Android), collaborating with the Performance Team, Data Team, and Product Leadership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Advanced SQL (BigQuery/Redash), proficiency in data visualization using AI tooling, and experience with statistical analysis (e.g., Pearson’s correlation, multivariate analysis). Knowledge of Rust/C++ is a strong plus. Strong proficiency with AI tools like Claude Code, Codex, or similar is highly desirable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Ability to understand browser component interactions and their impact on user experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Proven ability to work independently, translating technical requirements into business insights.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Independent problem solving:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; Comfortable working in unfamiliar technical problem spaces and figuring out a path forward with minimal guidance, using documentation, experimentation, source code, data, and other available resources&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Ranges:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Canada Tier 1 Locations&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$93,450&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$124,600 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Canada Tier 2 Locations&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$84,600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$112,800 CAD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Ranges:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Remote Germany&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€62.100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€82.800 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Ranges:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Remote UK&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£58,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£78,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/mozilla/contract-sr-data-analyst-sqltelemetrybrowser-engine-467983","tags":["Firefox"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1792659320},{"slug":"product-manager-english-french-berlin-berlin-319659","company_name":"unframe","title":"Product Manager (English/French)","description":"&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Unframe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unframe is an AI-first startup helping the world’s largest enterprises bring LLM-powered applications to life in days - not months. We combine the speed of a product company with the flexibility of a consultancy, helping customers move from idea to deployed AI systems faster than anyone else in the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by Bessemer, Craft, and TLV Partners with $100M in Series B funding, we’re building a fast-growing, revenue-generating company working with Fortune 500 customers globally&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on the front line: you engage directly with enterprise clients, lead discovery to uncover core business challenges, and design and ship tailored AI solutions built on Unframe&#39;s platform. You own the work end-to-end, serving as the strategic and technical bridge from initial conversation through to final deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a true builder role. You write the precise specifications and prompt architectures that bring solutions to life, making the critical design decisions that determine whether an enterprise AI deployment actually succeeds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a project-led role with unmediated access to clients at every stage. You will typically manage several engagements simultaneously, with short planning horizons and evolving requirements. Roughly 30 to 40 percent of the role is active client management, ensuring senior stakeholders remain aligned through delivery, progress reviews, and post-deployment rollouts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Enterprise Discovery: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct discovery sessions directly with enterprise clients to map workflows, uncover business challenges, and distinguish surface-level requests from fundamental operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design &amp;amp; Spec AI Solutions: &lt;/strong&gt;Translate customer problems into structured solution plans on Unframe&#39;s platform. Write detailed specs and define prompt and context structures, owning the complete solution design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive End-to-End Delivery: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with engineers and AI specialists to deliver solutions on target. Prioritize requirements and manage tradeoffs across speed, stability, and scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent the User &amp;amp; Platform: &lt;/strong&gt;Act as the voice of enterprise operators and domain experts while collaborating with the Platform team to identify reusable product patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in product management or technical delivery roles, with a proven track record working alongside engineering teams on complex, fast-paced technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Bilingual Fluency (English &amp;amp; French):&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent in French to connect with users and stakeholders in France, and fluent in English for daily collaboration across our international teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer-Led Discovery: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven experience personally leading consultative conversations with enterprise buyers and operators - not supporting a sales call, not interviewing platform users, but owning the conversation to surface unstated needs and translate them into clear solution scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Stakeholder Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to manage senior client relationships through a complex delivery; keeping stakeholders aligned, navigating competing priorities, and being the primary point of contact when requirements shift or timelines compress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-to-Solution Design: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to start from a raw business problem without existing features for reference, defining exactly how an AI solution should function and writing precise specs for build teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Delivery Execution: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience shipping AI-powered features under tight timelines, managing evolving requirements, and documenting strategic tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Solutions Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Direct exposure to building with LLMs - writing prompt structures, defining context and output constraints, working with agentic systems, or managing model uncertainty in a shipped product or working prototype. This is the dimension most learnable on the job; concrete work product carries more weight than certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Builder Orientation: &lt;/strong&gt;Driven by creating customer-facing solutions rather than simply managing traditional roadmaps or processing requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong written communication, systems thinking, high attention to detail, fluent English (written and verbal), and the ability to navigate multi-faceted projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Why join us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;At Unframe, you’ll help build AI systems that are already delivering real value to global enterprises - not prototypes, demos, or side projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;You’ll work with exceptional teammates, collaborate directly with top-tier customers, and have real influence over both the solutions we ship and the evolution of our platform. This is a hands-on, high-impact role where product thinking, technical depth, and creativity come together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;If you enjoy solving hard problems, moving fast, and building practical AI products that actually make it to production - we’d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/unframe/product-manager-english-french-berlin-berlin-319659","tags":["Product Growth"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin, Berlin","created_at":1792659318},{"slug":"growth-lead-berlin-214002","company_name":"Almedia","title":"Growth Lead (Berlin)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">This isn’t your regular job. Almedia is a place where those who want to push harder can accelerate their careers faster than anywhere else. We’re aiming to become Germany’s second bootstrapped unicorn. Almedia is already Europe’s #3 fastest-growing company in 2025 (FT1000).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building the future of marketing by rewarding our community of over 95 million users for engaging with our advertisers’ products. We are offering a new way to acquire users for the biggest companies in the world.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>At Almedia, you’ll:</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own way more, way earlier</strong> — you’ll be trusted with responsibility fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Push harder, get further</strong> — this isn’t a 9–5. We highly reward intensity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Join a rare environment</strong> — you will work with ambitious high-speed, high-ownership people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fully present</strong> — we’re 5 days a week in the office to build the energising momentum we need.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Growth Lead (Berlin)</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary: </strong>100-120k</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a powerhouse <strong>Growth Lead (Berlin)</strong> to become the a dedicated leader for our Growth (sales and account management) team. Reporting directly to the Growth Director and in close alignment with the CEO, you will be the architect of our go-to-market engine. This is a dual-impact role: you will lead, coach, and motivate a high-performing team while remaining "in the trenches" to close strategic partnerships with the world’s top mobile game publishers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own end-to-end growth by building a high-accountability team culture and a repeatable GTM playbook. You will turn publisher insights into product strategy, move fast to scale our outbound motion, and raise the bar on execution across the entire lifecycle—from first contact to long-term integration and partnership.</p><h2></h2><h2>What You’ll Do  🎯</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Architect the GTM Playbook:</strong> Build and own a repeatable outbound sales motion. You’ll define our segmentation, messaging, and CRM workflows to ensure the team executes with speed and precision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead from the Front:</strong> Personally drive Tier-1 deals from discovery to signed integration. You will land key accounts that serve as the "win stories" to unlock the rest of the market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale &amp; Mentor the Team:</strong> Manage, motivate, and develop a part of the Growth team. You’ll be responsible for their KPIs, career growth plans, and day-to-day coaching to foster a culture of extreme ownership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridge Product &amp; Market:</strong> Create a tight feedback loop with Product and Engineering. You will translate publisher needs into a prioritized backlog, ensuring our roadmap is aligned with what the market actually buys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational Excellence:</strong> Define the rituals of success—qualification standards, pipeline hygiene, and forecasting. You will provide the Growth Director with a live, transparent view of deal health and unblock the team to keep opportunities moving.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What your first 90 days look like</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Days 1–30:</strong> Shadow our Senior Growth Managers on their account calls. Take over 2 small accounts (sub-€10K daily spend) and learn the backbone of our growth engine hands-on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Days 31–60:</strong> Take over a full book of accounts. Own your first KPI review with our a senior team member. Contribute with your first written process improvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Days 61–90:</strong> Operating with increasing independence. You've caught at least one issue before it escalated and proposed a test or lever on your book.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Beyond 90 days:</strong> A clear path from Growth Lead to Strategic Growth Lead with even more ownership, and beyond.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What You’ll Bring 💡</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The "Player-Coach" DNA:</strong> You have a proven track record of running full-cycle enterprise sales (prospect → pitch → close) while simultaneously managing a small team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline Mastery:</strong> You know how to build an outbound engine from scratch. You are comfortable experimenting with A/B outreach, sequencing, and offer tests to find what sticks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Communication:</strong> You can translate complex product features into quantified ROI for Monetization and LiveOps leaders at major game studios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-Stakes Leadership:</strong> You give candid feedback, address performance early, and know how to keep a remote or multi-geo team (Berlin/China/Israel) engaged and hungry.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operational Rigor:</strong> You don’t just "do sales"—you build systems. You are a power user of CRM data and live by pipeline hygiene.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What Makes You a Great Fit 🌟</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own Everything:</strong> You care deeply about the team's performance and see every roadblock as an opportunity to build a better process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Move Fast:</strong> You thrive in the ambiguity of an early-stage environment and can pivot strategies without losing momentum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Focus on Impact:</strong> You prioritize the 20% of activities that drive 80% of the revenue. You are obsessed with results, not just "being busy."</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Why Almedia? 🎁</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scale With Almedia:</strong> Have a real impact and grow alongside a startup that has been profitable from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-Growth Environment:</strong> We encourage all staff to take ownership of projects and consistently raise the bar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Do More, Get More:</strong> Generous bonus scheme to ensure great, proactive work is valued.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in fostering talent, evaluating all skill levels during the hiring process, and providing a clear path for growth. Almedia is an equal opportunity employer. We embrace and celebrate diversity, and encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply.</p><hr><p>Compensation: €100K – €120K</p><ul><li> • €100K – €120K</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/almedia/growth-lead-berlin-214002","tags":["Growth"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792658447},{"slug":"event-community-manager-ai-x-greentech-berlin-219897","company_name":"Reonic","title":"Event & Community Manager (AI x Greentech) (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You make Reonic impossible to miss. Plan it, fill it, own it.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Looking for a role where every event is yours from first idea to last guest out the door? This is for you! You’ll own our trade shows, speaker events, and internal team moments end to end, working closely with Marketing, Sales, and the founders. If you get your energy from people and love making things happen under pressure, this is built for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Please note that for this role, C2 German and C2 English proficiency are required. This is a full-time, on-site position based in Berlin.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>End-to-end trade show ownership.</strong> From picking the right shows to booth concept, logistics, and on-site execution, you run it all and make sure Reonic stands out on even the busiest floor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speaker events that fill the room.</strong> You find and book the right speakers, build the program, promote it, and make sure the right people show up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer and partner relationships.</strong> You’re the face of Reonic at events: confident with customers, partners, and speakers, and the one who turns a conversation into a lasting connection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Internal team moments.</strong> From offsites to celebrations, you create the experiences that bring our people together and keep our culture strong as we grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial impact.</strong> You don’t just run events, you make them count. You work with Sales and Marketing to turn events into pipeline, partnerships, and brand awareness, then measure what actually works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speed and adaptability.</strong> Tight timelines and shifting priorities are part of the job. You keep things moving and deliver anyway.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Makes You a Great Fit</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Native or C2-level German and C2-level English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience running trade shows end to end, ideally in B2B or software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of booking speakers and organizing events people actually want to attend.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Outgoing and confident, energized rather than drained by customers, partners, and speakers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly organized with a hands-on mentality. You sweat the details without losing sight of the big picture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You thrive in fast-paced environments and don’t slow down when plans change last minute.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be part of one of the fastest growing VC-backed startups in Germany with 3000+ satisfied B2B customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A vibrant, collaborative office culture where great ideas happen face-to-face. We’re a full in-person team (5 days/week) in a beautiful Berlin office near Hackescher Markt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy opportunities for personal and professional growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embrace the freedom to innovate and make quick changes in a dynamic team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perks include gym membership or Deutschlandticket, Uber Eats after 7pm, Uber home after 7:30pm, regular team events, and a MacBook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Receive competitive pay.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Even if you don’t meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply! Imposter syndrome shouldn’t hold you back. We value talent and passion above all.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Reonic</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Reonic, we’re on a mission to simplify renewable technology with our AI operating system for renewable installers. Backed by top-tier investors and trusted by 3000+ business customers, we’re growing fast, and we need YOU to help us accommodate our new and existing customers.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/reonic/event-community-manager-ai-x-greentech-berlin-219897","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792658425},{"slug":"security-engineer-munich-486071","company_name":"Proxima Fusion GmbH","title":"Security Engineer","description":"<h3><strong>WHO WE ARE</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proxima Fusion is Europe’s fastest-growing fusion company and the continent’s best-funded fusion player, as well as the first spin-out from the Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics (IPP). Backed by over €650M and powered by a growing team across Munich, Zurich, and Oxford, we are developing the hardware and infrastructure needed to deliver the world’s first commercial stellarator fusion power plant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our concept advances the most mature fusion technology out there, the Wendelstein 7-X stellarator, through two next-generation machines: Alpha and Stellaris. Our work combines stellarator optimization, advanced computation, machine learning, and high-temperature superconducting magnets to unlock higher-performance designs that were previously out of reach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turning these designs into a functioning fusion power plant requires excellence and ownership across every discipline, from physics and engineering to software, manufacturing, law, and business functions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>WHY JOIN US</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work on a civilisation-scale problem </strong>- Clean, baseload fusion energy is one of the few genuinely world-changing challenges, and every hire directly accelerates the path to a working stellarator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow as fast as the company does</strong> - With headcount set to roughly 5x in a few years and major technical milestones ahead on the path to our demo machine and first power plant, your role grows under you; today's hire is tomorrow's function lead.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tackle problems that don't exist elsewhere</strong> - Fusion sits at a rare intersection of deep-tech R&amp;D, industrial procurement, government relations, and venture financing, so non-tech functions face challenges no other workplace can offer.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>YOUR IMPACT</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Senior Security Engineer in Munich, you will own security implementation and security monitoring, digital and physical, for a company building one of the most valuable bodies of fusion IP in Europe. Protecting it is its own challenge, and you are the person who will own it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>WHAT YOU WILL DO</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Build out our security monitoring capability: select and run the SIEM, decide what's worth alerting on, and tune out the noise.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Own incident response end-to-end, from investigation through to a post-mortem and a fix that holds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Harden the environment hands-on across endpoint and EDR, identity and access, network, and infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Finish maturing Zero Trust: identity and device posture as joint conditions for access, and MFA everywhere.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Handle the long tail of edge cases that comes with a fast-growing team and a lot of contractors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Secure our Google-centric workplace, where most of our IP moves — DLP, data classification and labeling, retention, and context-aware access.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Secure the software supply chain in collaboration with our platform team: source control, access boundaries, secrets, and CI/CD.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Run vulnerability and attack surface management, and drive remediation to be done with the teams that own the systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Set and monitor our physical security standard with Business Operations, who implement it on site: access zones, CCTV and alerting, visitor and contractor access, and site access as one joiner-mover-leaver process with digital access, across multiple locations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Give our compliance work the technical substance it needs: evidence, remediation, and support through audits and pen tests.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must have</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     You have 5+ years hands-on in security engineering, with real depth in identity, endpoint, and infrastructure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     You have built or substantially operated a SIEM, and run real incidents end-to-end.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     You have implemented Zero Trust in production - unified IdP and MDM, conditional access, device posture.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     You know Google Workspace Enterprise security well, or can get there fast from an equivalent platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     You are automation-first: Terraform, and scripting in Python, Bash, or PowerShell are no strangers to you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     You are fluent in CIS Benchmarks, NIST, ISO 27001, and NIS2 without being ruled by them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     You can turn a technical finding into a business impact and actionable solutions</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Interest or a track record in AI security.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Hands-on cloud and container security: GCP, containers, Kubernetes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Certifications such as CISSP, GCIA, GCIH, CCSP, or Google Cloud Professional Cloud Security Engineer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">•     Experience in a regulated, export-controlled, or high-security environment, where physical and digital security meet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>INTERVIEW PROCESS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter Interview (30-60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Screening (30 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Panel (3x60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CEO call (30 min)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>This role sits at L2/L3 of our framework, please inquire during the recruitment process for further information</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Proxima Fusion, our mission is bold: making limitless clean energy a reality. To get there, we need a high-performing, diverse team that brings different perspectives, challenges assumptions, and builds together with purpose. We know that diversity of thought and experience leads to better ideas, stronger execution, and a more resilient team. We don’t look at how you identify, what you look like, who you choose to worship or what ethnicity you are. We care about what you can bring to the table.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/proxima-fusion-gmbh/security-engineer-munich-486071","tags":["Business Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792658424},{"slug":"lead-rd-engineer-tritium-breeding-blanket-munich-53731","company_name":"Proxima Fusion GmbH","title":"Lead R&D Engineer, Tritium-Breeding Blanket","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO WE ARE</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proxima Fusion is Europe’s fastest-growing fusion company and the continent’s best-funded fusion player, as well as the first spin-out from the Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics (IPP). Backed by over €650M and powered by a growing team across Munich, Zurich, and Oxford, we are developing the hardware and infrastructure needed to deliver the world’s first commercial stellarator fusion power plant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our concept advances the most mature fusion technology out there, the Wendelstein 7-X stellarator, through two next-generation machines: Alpha and Stellaris. Our work combines stellarator optimization, advanced computation, machine learning, and high-temperature superconducting magnets to unlock higher-performance designs that were previously out of reach.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turning these designs into a functioning fusion power plant requires excellence and ownership across every discipline, from physics and engineering to software, manufacturing, law, and business functions.<br /><br /><strong>TEAM AND ROLE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the architecture of the world’s first commercial fusion power plant</strong> – Own system-level decisions that determine how a first-of-a-kind energy technology is designed, integrated, and ultimately deployed at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solve some of the most complex engineering challenges in industry</strong> – Work across tightly coupled disciplines (plasma physics, magnets, cryogenics, manufacturing, controls, and more) to resolve critical trade-offs and turn cutting-edge science into a functioning product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build real hardware with a pragmatic, fast-moving team from all over the world</strong> – Combine advanced simulation and systems thinking with a strong execution mindset, focusing on practical engineering solutions that accelerate the path to commercial fusion energy.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHY JOIN PROXIMA FUSION</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will get to work on some of the most complex tech challenges to bring abundant, safe, clean energy to the world.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get to join and learn from an exceptional selection of accomplished and driven individuals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do your life’s best work and enjoy the journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Get to show that big things are possible in Europe when you assemble the best talent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>YOUR IMPACT</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Lead R&amp;D Engineer for the Stellaris tritium-breeding blanket, you will build and lead Proxima Fusion’s blanket development from initial concept to first prototype tests. You will translate a defined R&amp;D budget into a small set of parallel breeder-blanket concepts, developed rapidly with external research and industrial partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote maintainability is a fundamental part of the blanket architecture from day one. Each concept must be thought with the power plant architecture in mind and demonstrate how blanket modules can be installed, connected, inspected, replaced and recovered remotely.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The objective is to leverage existing public research, challenge the most consequential assumptions, learn from hardware quickly and iterate to a functional blanket concept for our future commercial plant fleet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT YOU WILL DO</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the blanket design from initial requirements through conceptual design, prototype manufacture and testing, with accountability for budget, schedule and technical outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the integrated remote-maintenance architecture for each concept, including segmentation, access, handling, service connections, inspection, replacement and recovery from failed operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the compliance analysis across neutronics, thermal hydraulics, structural integrity, materials, tritium, decommissioning, safety and remote maintenance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the rapid fail-fast prototype: select what to test and lead its design, procurement, manufacture, instrumentation, commissioning and test campaign on ambitious timelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the translation of test results into updated models, requirements, risk assessments and design decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and build the multidisciplinary, technical design team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO YOU ARE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Master’s degree or higher in mechanical engineering, nuclear engineering, materials science, chemical engineering, physics or equivalent experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have led the development of complex nuclear, thermal, chemical or energy technology from conceptual design into hardware and testing, under budget and time constraints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to lead multidisciplinary trade studies without converging prematurely on a preferred solution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge in several relevant domains, such as thermal hydraulics, structural mechanics, neutronics, nuclear materials, tritium systems, high-temperature coolants, corrosion, manufacturing or remote handling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to distinguish between analysis that enables a decision and analysis that merely adds detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable structuring and managing technical work with external institutes, industrial partners and specialist suppliers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willing to test critical assumptions early, learn from failure and stop weak development paths.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to make clear and defensible engineering decisions under uncertainty.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with fusion blankets, fission-reactor components, breeder materials, tritium systems or remotely maintained nuclear equipment are an advantage, but are explicitly not necessary.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>INTERVIEW PROCESS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter Interview (30-60 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Screening (30 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Panel (3x60 min)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Proxima Fusion, our mission is bold: making limitless clean energy a reality. To get there, we need a high-performing, diverse team that brings different perspectives, challenges assumptions, and builds together with purpose. We know that diversity of thought and experience leads to better ideas, stronger execution, and a more resilient team. We don’t look at how you identify, what you look like, who you choose to worship or what ethnicity you are. We care about what you can bring to the table.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/proxima-fusion-gmbh/lead-rd-engineer-tritium-breeding-blanket-munich-53731","tags":["Stellarator Architecture","Plasma Modelling & Research","Numerical Optimization"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1792658424},{"slug":"customer-service-advisor-berlin-413011","company_name":"BSI Merch GmbH","title":"Customer Service Advisor","description":"<h2><strong>About BSI </strong></h2><p>BSI Merch & Artist Services runs design, supply, fulfilment and e-commerce for artists and their labels and management. We build and run official artist web stores on Shopify for the UK and EU, ship from our warehouses in Leamington Spa and Berlin, and support album campaigns from pre-order through to release week, for artists including Franz Ferdinand, Kneecap, Frank Turner and We Are Palace. </p><p>Every order through those stores is a fan buying something from an artist they care about. Customer Services is where that relationship is won or lost. </p><h2><strong>The Role </strong></h2><p>You'll answer customers across our artist stores, resolve order, delivery and returns issues end to end, and feed what you learn back to the wider e-commerce team so problems get fixed at the source. </p><h2>What we are looking for</h2><p>You bring professional experience in customer service, clear communication skills, and a practical approach to resolving support requests in a fast-paced environment.</p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities </strong></h2><p><strong>Customer support</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Respond to customer tickets by email and chat through Gorgias, across multiple artist stores and in each store's tone. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Handle order queries end to end: tracking, delivery delays, address changes, missing items, pre-order dates and cancellations. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Manage returns, exchanges, refunds and reships, including damaged and faulty items, collecting photo evidence and processing returns through Loop Returns. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Resolve complaints fairly and within our service standards (acknowledgement within 2 working days, resolution within 14 calendar days), escalating to the CS Lead where needed. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Apply UK and EU consumer rights correctly, including the 14-day cancellation period and its exceptions. </p></li></ul><p><strong>Working with the wider team</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Chase stock and fulfilment issues with the warehouse and Product team, and flag anything that needs a reship or a hold on stock. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Raise patterns early to the Head of Customer Service and/or relevant department </p></li></ul><p><strong>Housekeeping and reporting</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Keep the queue clean: tag tickets accurately, close spam and auto-replies, and keep macros and Help Centre articles up to date where required. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Log refunds, reships, common issues and recurring problems so they feed into the monthly CS report for each client. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Help maintain and improve the AI Agent's guidance and the CS Help Centre for new stores. </p></li></ul><p><strong>Launches and release weeks </strong></p><p>Our workload follows the music. A store launch, a pre-sale or an album release can bring hundreds of tickets in a few days, and the questions shift with each stage of the campaign. </p><ul><li><p><strong>Pre-order and pre-access:</strong> questions about access codes, dispatch dates and what's included in bundles. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>Release week:</strong> high volume around delivery timing, signed items and chart-eligible bundles, where getting media to customers on time matters. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p><strong>After release:</strong> returns, damaged items, missing parcels and reship requests. </p></li></ul><p>You'll need to stay calm and accurate under pressure, prioritise the tickets that matter most, and occasionally flex your hours around a launch. </p><p><strong>Skills and experience </strong></p><p><strong>Essential</strong> </p><ul><li><p>At least 1 year in customer service, ideally for an e-commerce or retail brand. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Clear, warm written English and German, with the judgement to adjust tone for different artists and fanbases. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Comfortable working a busy ticket queue and hitting response times. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Organised and detail-focused: order numbers, SKUs, addresses and refunds need to be right first time. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Confident using helpdesk software and picking up new systems quickly. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Knows when to resolve and when to escalate. </p></li></ul><p><strong>Desirable</strong> </p><ul><li><p>Experience with Gorgias, Shopify or Loop Returns. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Knowledge of UK and EU consumer rights for online purchases. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Experience in music, merchandise or entertainment retail. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>An interest in music and the artists we work with. </p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Work with a wide range of artists, from emerging acts to established names</p></li><li><p>A great, fast-growing team</p></li><li><p>A modern office in Kreuzberg</p></li><li><p>Discounts on a monthly BVG ticket and Urban Sports Club membership</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/bsi-merch-gmbh/customer-service-advisor-berlin-413011","tags":["Customer Service"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1792657921},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-java-igaming-334472","company_name":"Xdesign","title":"Senior Software Engineer (Java) iGaming","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Working at CreateFuture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://createfuture.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CreateFuture&lt;/a&gt; is an&amp;nbsp;AI-native consulting partner&amp;nbsp;where people do work that matters and are supported to do it well. We work alongside organisations such as PayPal, adidas, NatWest, FanDuel and Money Saving Expert, building digital products and services that make a difference&amp;nbsp; while always putting people first.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
