r of attorney cases and SME customers who might have complex needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">To proactively identify areas for process improvement and to seek new and innovative ways to better serve the customer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">To live and breathe the Bank’s values, representing the Bank to customers and speaking to customers in a way that resonates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">To support other teams as appropriate, where customer communication or engagement is required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Personal Attributes &amp; Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong customer service experience, having worked in customer facing and or telephone service roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using core banking systems and familiar with the use and application of social media as a form of interaction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in dealing with complex complaints and in taking ownership of customer concerns through to resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience of core processes (e.g. account opening, servicing and closing, payments processing, complaint handling, KYC case referrals, general enquiry management).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in working with workflow / task management tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of financial services rules and guidelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent oral and written skills as they will be constantly communicating with customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enthusiastic and articulate, whilst being motivated by a need to help people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A problem solver and can create positive customer outcomes in diverse situations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conform to our ethical standards and conduct.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform administrative tasks related to the customer interaction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver outstanding customer service as measured through customer satisfaction KPIs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage and monitor service providers for customer quality.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive customer service innovation and continuous improvement of process to deliver better customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as an ambassador/advocate for Customer within the Bank.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adhere to quality control requirements and ensure compliance with policy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working at Allica Bank</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Allica Bank we want to ensure our employees have the right tools and environment in which to succeed in their role and in support of our customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our employees are at the heart of everything we do, so our benefits are designed with you in mind:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full onboarding support and continued development opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Options for flexible working</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular social activities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discretionary bonus scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private health cover</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Life assurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Family friendly policies including enhanced Maternity &amp; Paternity leave</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Don’t tick every box?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Don’t worry if you don’t have all the skills or requirements listed on the job description. If you think you’ll be a good fit, we’d still love to hear from you!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible working</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know the ‘9-to-5’ isn’t right for everyone. That’s why Allica Bank is fully committed to flexible and hybrid working. Please let us know what is best for you and, if we can, we will do our best to accommodate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a diverse bunch here at Allica, with all kinds of experiences, backgrounds and lifestyles. Our openness and differences make us stronger, and we want everybody to feel comfortable bringing as much of themselves to work with them as they like.</p><hr><p>Compensation: £25K – £27K • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li> • Band 1 £25K – £27K • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/allica-bank/customer-service-advisor-milton-keynes-177594","tags":["Lending & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Milton Keynes Office","created_at":1792680019},{"slug":"accounts-assistant-london-446891","company_name":"Comind","title":"Accounts Assistant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At CoMind, we are developing a non-invasive neuromonitoring technology that will result in a new era of clinical brain monitoring. In joining us, you will be helping to create cutting-edge technologies that will improve how we diagnose and treat brain disorders, ultimately improving and saving the lives of patients across the world.</p><h3><br /><strong>The Role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an Accounts Assistant to join our small, hands-on finance team at a London hardware technology startup that's growing fast. You'll keep our day-to-day finances running smoothly, from payables and supplier relationships to cash management and month-end. You'll also own the finance tools we rely on, including Xero, ApprovalMax, Expensify and Dext. In a team this size, your work is visible and your ideas count: we want you to spot what could work better and use automation and AI to build it. Please note applicants must be based in the UK and have the right to work in the UK.<br /></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">All accounts payable tasks, including invoice coding, preparing weekly payment runs and resolving queries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete daily bank and debit card reconciliations using Xero</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor bank accounts and prepare transfers to keep operational accounts sufficiently funded</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Send a weekly cash status report to senior management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with month-end tasks including accruals, prepayments and balance sheet reconciliations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up new suppliers and act as the main point of contact for supplier invoice and payment queries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Administer our finance apps (including ApprovalMax, Expensify and Dext), managing users, approval workflows and integrations with Xero</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and implement improvements to finance processes, with a focus on automation and making good use of AI<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is fundamental to our culture. It's not just a tool, but a core part of how we work, collaborate, and innovate. We expect all team members to embrace AI in their daily work and continuously find new ways to use it effectively.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Skills &amp; Experience:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience as an accounts assistant, accounts payable assistant or cash management assistant</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using Xero</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: AAT qualified, or studying<br /></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company equity plan so all employees share in the success of the company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salary-sacrifice pension scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private medical, dental and vision insurance (medical history disregarded)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Group life insurance at 4x annual income</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive mental health support, including unlimited access to 1:1 sessions with trained professionals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited holiday allowance (+ bank holidays) and one week of remote working per quarter</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch voucher (£10) every day for JustEat and free dinner on those days where you need to work later</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Twice weekly deliveries of fresh fruit and an extensive selection of snacks and drinks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">YuLife subscription, allowing you to turn your daily steps and meditation into discounts at a range of stores</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Disclaimer</strong> - We use Granola, an AI notetaker, throughout our interview process to help capture notes. It's used only for note-taking during the conversation. Transcripts aren't saved to shared drives or stored externally. Let us know if you'd prefer we don't.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: £33K – £41K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £33K – £41K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/comind/accounts-assistant-london-446891","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1792680019},{"slug":"manager-compliance-advisory-and-data-protection-london-194533","company_name":"Griffin","title":"Manager: Compliance Advisory and Data Protection","description":"<h2><strong>About Griffin</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi, we’re Griffin. We’re a fully regulated UK bank that powers the accounts and payments offerings of product-led fintechs and platforms like Uber, Yonder, Prosper, and Sidekick. By doing the heavy lifting behind the scenes, our customers can focus on what they do best - delivering amazing customer experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve grown rapidly since our launch in 2024, and today provide the banking backbone behind products in remittance, payroll, wealth, insurance, proptech, payments, neobanking and more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re moving into card issuing, stablecoin infrastructure, and agentic finance next as we continue to support the next generation of product-led companies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://griffin.com">Learn more about what we do</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Our culture</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that smart, motivated, conscientious people thrive in high-trust, high-autonomy environments and have done our best to create such an environment at Griffin. People who thrive here don’t require much hand-holding, and go out of their way to figure out how to contribute in the most valuable way possible.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've been remote-first since we were established in 2017 and we remain so today. Work here is asynchronous and fully flexible - because we want to be a part of your life in a way that helps you to get the most out of both your work <em>and</em> home life.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We understand that our culture and ways of working aren’t for everyone, and we’re very intentional about our hiring process as a result. We won't hire people who don’t seem like a strong fit for our core values, even if they're otherwise extremely qualified.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our strong culture has helped us to remain a mission-driven company as we have scaled, and gives our people a clear, explicit operating framework and the space to focus on delivering real value for our customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://griffin.com/culture">Learn more about our culture.</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join our Service guild and work across first line operations, sales and produt. Working closely with Protect (our second line) you'll be the first person dedicated to compliance within the team. You'll define what great compliance solutions look like. Then implement them , keeping Griffin's products and customer outcomes in shape as we grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want compliance and data protection built into how we design, sell and run our products. As our hands on DPO and compliance adviser, in the first line (the teams who run the business and own its risks), you'll bring regulatory expertise to help our operations, commercial and product teams do exactly that. With card issuing and other launches coming up, there's plenty to get stuck into.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What success looks like</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first year, you’ve taken ownership of our data protection agenda. You’ve gone looking for ways to improve, made the changes happen, and given our senior leaders an honest picture of where we stand. You’ve sought out our operations, sales and product teams and shown them that working with you makes things smoother, not slower. Now they bring you in early by default. You’ve guided at least one major launch, like card issuing, from first idea to go live. And you’ve put clear governance and outcome monitoring in place for our live products, so Protect (our second line risk and compliance team) sees fewer surprises and finds a stronger compliance foundation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>To do this you'll be involved in:</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product development:</strong> turning regulation into clear requirements, customer journeys, T&amp;Cs and fair value assessments, from first idea through product approval to launch, with data protection built in from the start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product lifecycle management:</strong> keeping live products compliant through periodic fair value assessments, outcome monitoring, reviews, changes and closures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sales:</strong> helping our commercial team check early whether potential partners fit our risk appetite, and reviewing sales material.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Marketing:</strong> working on marketing materials, both ours and our customers’, to make sure they comply with regulation and our own policies, and that our financial promotions are properly challenged.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Service (Operations):</strong> building regulatory and data protection requirements into how Service works day to day, with procedures and controls people actually use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Regulatory change: </strong>working out what new rules mean for us, and making sure the right teams make the right changes on time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Issues and reporting: </strong>investigating and fixing compliance issues, including personal data breaches, and reporting clearly on compliance risks and customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working with second line (Protect): </strong>bringing them in early, sharing the evidence they need, and acting on their challenge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data protection:</strong> being our Data Protection Officer (DPO), which means:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">advising our teams on their obligations, including data protection impact assessments (DPIAs) and transfer risk assessments (TRAs)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">monitoring and auditing how well we comply with the UK GDPR, other data protection laws and our own policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">training colleagues and raising awareness of data protection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">being our contact point for the ICO and for people with questions or requests about their data</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our DPO, you’ll report directly to our COO and have the independence you need to do the job well. We’ll involve you early in anything that affects personal data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We expect you to shape this role: This description reflects what we need today. How you achieve these outcomes, where you focus your energy, how this role evolves is for you to define as you learn what our customers need and where you can make the biggest difference.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We expect you to shape this role:</strong> This description reflects what we need today. How you achieve these outcomes, where you focus your energy, how this role evolves—that's for you to define as you learn what our customers need and where our technical gaps are.</p><h2></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your background</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We need a proactive doer. You get stuck in without waiting to be asked, and you’re comfortable tackling regulations you haven’t met before. You use your experience and expertise to help our teams find simple, clear and compliant solutions. Your advice is balanced, easy to follow and focused on the risks that matter most. You want to push the business forward, and you see good compliance as part of how we get there.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To ensure this, we're looking for people who have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance experience</strong> in the first (preferred) or second line of a UK regulated firm, ideally a bank, e-money institution or payments firm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Practical knowledge of the rules behind our products</strong>, like Consumer Duty, BCOBS, CASS, FISMA, the Payment Services Regulations and the Money Laundering Regulations. As well as familiarity with HMRC requirements like BBSI and AEOI reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expert knowledge of data protection law and practice</strong>, including the UK GDPR, the Data Protection Act 2018, PECR and the Data (Use and Access) Act 2025.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on experience turning regulation into practical requirements</strong> for product, sales or operations teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A curious, questioning approach.</strong> You know the right questions to ask before signing something off, not just the rules to check it against.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The confidence to challenge,</strong> clearly and kindly, when something isn’t right.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A love of writing</strong>. We have a major amount of written documentation that you will be contributing to, and we place a high degree of importance on clarity and readability (you can find out more here about <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://griffin.com/how-we-write">how we write</a>).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally, you would also:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Have deep expertise in at least one specialist area,</strong> such as payments, cards, Consumer Duty, BCOBS, financial promotions or similar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Have been a DPO,</strong> or worked closely with one, in a regulated firm.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Have worked in finance or banking.</strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What can we offer you?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an early stage startup and we're working hard to expand our benefits package. We're planning to add to this list in the future.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary:</strong> £ 80-90 (DOE)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first flexibility:</strong> Work from anywhere in the UK</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work from abroad:</strong> Up to 20 days a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off:</strong> 25 days’ holiday, bank holidays and a winter break (we shut down between Christmas and New Year)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Share options:</strong> Own a part of what we’re building together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension:</strong> Auto-enrolment into our Penfold scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Insurance:</strong> Private medical with Bupa (including family cover) and life insurance with AIG</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wellbeing:</strong> 1:1 coaching and therapy session available through Oliva</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family leave:</strong> Enhanced parental leave with up to 6 months on full pay after two years’ service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI tools:</strong> Everyone has a Claude subscription on us and access to other premium tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your setup:</strong> We’ll support you in creating a comfortable and effective WFH environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>As a bank, we’re committed to maintaining the highest standards of security. This means that the successful candidate will need to complete background screening, and our offer will be conditional upon satisfactory review of these checks. This would include verification of right to work, criminal record, credit history, social media and professional reference checks</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2></h2><h2><strong>How long will the process take?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We move as fast as possible, but it normally takes us about 2-3 weeks to get to know to each other.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 1:</strong> An initial phone call with our Talent Team for us to tell you more about Griffin and learn about your recent experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Meet your manager to talk through your experience and how that relates to the requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 3:</strong> A task based on what you’ll be doing on a day to day at Griffin.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 4:</strong> Meet with peers in your team for a more in-depth technical interview.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Step 5</strong>: Culture and Founder interview: Learn more about this <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://griffin.com/blog/how-to-design-culture-interviews">here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>How do I apply?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are we your next move? Apply via the link below, if there's a match our Talent team will reach out to schedule an initial conversation and talk you through what happens next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>We’re remote-first</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We trust people to do great work wherever they are. We hire across the UK and most of our team works remotely full-time. We have a small London office in Moorgate for those who want it, and about a third of the company is close enough to use it occasionally, but there's no expectation to be there. What matters is the work, not where you do it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Under representation</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Griffin, we’re looking for people who instinctively vibe with our values, behaviours and mission. You’re encouraged to apply, even if your experience doesn’t tick every box. Careers, like life, can take many twists and turns. Your technical expertise and path to where you are today will stand out. We're committed to creating a place where everyone belongs and we welcome diverse perspectives, backgrounds and people who are ready to build a global platform for programmable finance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><em>Griffin Bank Ltd request that recruitment agencies do not speculatively submit CVs to any employee or associate of our company unless explicitly asked to do so by a member of our Talent team.</em></h3><h3><em>Any CVs sent to any member of our team on a speculative basis will not be recognised and we will not accept liability for any fee or commission should we subsequently employ a candidate who applied to us directly or was introduced by an instructed agency that may also have been submitted speculatively by an uninstructed agency.</em></h3><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/griffin/manager-compliance-advisory-and-data-protection-london-194533","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London or remote within the UK","created_at":1792680019},{"slug":"workforce-management-manager-cardiff-147883","company_name":"Veezu","title":"Workforce Management Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your role at Veezu:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Workforce Management (WFM) Manager is responsible for overseeing end-to-end workforce planning within a fast paced contact centre environment, with direct oversight of an offshore partner responsible for producing demand forecasts and staffing models. This role ensures forecast accuracy, optimal staffing levels, service level achievement and cost efficiency. The WFM Manager acts as the primary liaison between internal JBC (contact centre) Management and the offshore WFM team to ensure alignment on assumptions, performance expectations and continuous improvement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role ensures that our JBCs are staffed to operate with excellence, consistency &amp; efficiency, maximising booking performance, enhancing customer experience and driving success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who are Veezu?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Veezu is the UK's fastest growing taxi and private hire technology business operating across hundreds of UK towns and cities. We are a tech-driven on-demand mobility service that supports our hyper-local communities, helping them thrive and so much more!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The WFM Manager will provide leadership, guidance, and support to all Team Managers, acting as the central point of operational coordination and strategic alignment for JBC forecasting &amp; scheduling nationwide.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create a balance between cost efficiency &amp; service performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage shift patterns, holiday cover and absence planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Shift Managers to monitor live operational performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make in-day adjustments to staffing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage contingency planning for demand spikes and extreme weather.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>OFFSHORE VENDOR MANAGEMENT</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the relationship with the offshore WFM provider responsible for forecasting and capacity planning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review and validate forecasts produced by the offshore team (short-term, long-term, and budget forecasts).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure forecasting assumptions align with business drivers, marketing plans, seasonality, and growth projections.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive continuous improvement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Align offshore staffing models with UK demand forecasts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalate performance issues.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>FORECASTING &amp; CAPACITY PLANNING</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Approve weekly, monthly, and annual forecasts for contact volume, AHT, shrinkage, and FTE requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Challenge assumptions and drive continuous improvement in forecasting methodologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate with local JBC Management teams to maintain accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Head of / JBC Director on medium &amp; long term budgets and headcount modelling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify risks to over/under staffings.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SCHEDULING &amp; SERVICE LEVEL MANAGEMENT</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure schedules generated meet service level targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor intraday and real-time performance in partnership with Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee shrinkage, occupancy, and adherence performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalate risks related to under- or over-staffing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>PERFORMANCE REPORTING &amp; ANALYTICS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide reporting on service levels, forecast accuracy (volume, call to booking ratio, CPH &amp; AHT) and capacity utilisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify trends and recommend data-driven improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct root cause analysis on service level misses.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ACQUISITION GROWTH</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist the M&amp;A and Integration teams with the successful integration of newly acquired businesses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement agreed strategies and associated plans and ensure projects are delivered on schedule and meet agreed timescales, objectives, business needs and budget.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>COMPLIANCE</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the highest standards of Health &amp; Safety.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead by example and act in compliance with GDPR, information governance, our policies and area specific requirements at all times, supporting with training and auditing when required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be committed to maintaining our ISO27001 certification and set high standards for Information Security compliance.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll need:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a passion for planning &amp; forecasting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a deep understanding of call centre service level performance expectations while maintaining cost discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are analytical, data driven and results-oriented.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think strategically.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You lead by example and inspire others.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are an excellent communicator.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Where you’ll be:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is flexible on location (being one of the main Veezu Hubs) with a requirement to attend meetings at other Veezu office locations across the country as needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Veezu is committed to fair and inclusive recruitment, welcoming applications from all backgrounds, experiences, and communities.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/veezu/workforce-management-manager-cardiff-147883","tags":["Customer Support Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Cardiff HQ","created_at":1792680018},{"slug":"support-engineer-edinburgh-259530","company_name":"Wordsmith","title":"Support Engineer","description":"<h1><strong>Support Engineer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Edinburgh <br /></p><h2><strong>Wordsmith</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wordsmith is building the legal operating system for in-house teams, and we are growing fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in-house legal is becoming one of the most important functions in the AI era. Every business is moving faster, but legal work is still too often scattered across inboxes, chats, documents and disconnected systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wordsmith brings that work into one system. Requests come in from across the business, AI agents handle the routine, lawyers stay in control where judgement matters, and every step is captured as work happens.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are built for in-house legal, not law firms. Our goal is to help legal teams move faster, reduce unnecessary external counsel spend and become a function the business can run with.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">More than 500 companies, including Financial Times, Safelite, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Trip.com">Trip.com</a>, Canva, Starling and Sage, use Wordsmith. Backed by over $100M from Index Ventures, General Catalyst, Highland Europe and others, we are building one of the defining companies in legal AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring a Support Engineer to provide fast, thoughtful and technically rigorous help to Wordsmith customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll own technical questions and incidents from first response through to resolution. You’ll understand what the customer is trying to achieve, reproduce reported behaviour, investigate the underlying cause and explain the outcome clearly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is more than scripted customer support. You’ll be expected to investigate application behaviour at a technical level, including reading logs and tracing issues through the product and its codebase. Where appropriate to your experience, you may also propose and submit code fixes through our normal engineering review and release process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wordsmith supports customers globally through a follow-the-sun model. You’ll work the standard hours for your region and hand over unresolved issues clearly to colleagues in other regions. There is no routine expectation that you work another region’s hours.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own technical support requests — triage, investigate and resolve customer questions and incidents from first response to confirmed resolution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diagnose problems thoroughly — gather the right context, reproduce reported behaviour, inspect logs and data, and trace issues through the product and codebase.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resolve technical issues — correct configuration or usage problems directly and collaborate with Engineering when a product or infrastructure change is required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute code fixes where appropriate — depending on your experience, propose and submit well-tested fixes through the standard engineering review and deployment process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate clearly — give customers timely and accurate updates, explain technical issues without unnecessary jargon and set honest expectations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage escalations — bring in Engineering, Product or other specialists when needed while retaining ownership of the case and its communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support global handovers — document investigation, impact, current status and next actions so colleagues in another region can continue work without losing momentum.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Protect service quality — recognise high-impact incidents quickly, follow the appropriate escalation process and contribute to incident reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build customer knowledge — create and maintain troubleshooting guides, known-issue documentation and help-centre content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reduce repeat problems — identify patterns in support demand and recommend improvements to the product, documentation, tooling and customer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve support operations — help develop service levels, escalation paths, reporting and technical-support processes as the function scales.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in technical support, product support, software engineering, solutions engineering or another customer-facing technical role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong diagnostic ability — you can work methodically from symptoms to root cause rather than relying on guesswork.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A working understanding of modern web applications, APIs, authentication, integrations and common browser or network issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using diagnostic information such as application logs, monitoring tools, browser developer tools and database queries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enough familiarity with software code to navigate a codebase, follow application logic and use it to investigate reported behaviour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear customer communication — you can remain calm under pressure, set expectations honestly and explain complex issues at the right level of detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ownership — you remain responsible for moving an issue forward even when other teams need to contribute.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound prioritisation — you can assess urgency and customer impact and recognise when an issue requires immediate escalation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Care and precision — you document what you tested, avoid unsupported conclusions and confirm that the customer’s problem has actually been resolved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in AI systems — you’re curious about how AI-enabled products behave and comfortable investigating issues that may not always be deterministic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">No legal background is required, but you should be motivated to learn how in-house legal teams work.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Desirable, but not essential</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience writing and debugging production software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to create automated tests and submit code fixes for engineering review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting AI-enabled or data-intensive applications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with incident-management and observability tools.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an in-person team based in Edinburgh. You should expect to work from the office as your default.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We support customers globally using a follow-the-sun model. You’ll work the normal hours agreed for your region and create clear handovers when an issue needs to continue beyond them. Any exceptional on-call or out-of-hours arrangements would be agreed and communicated separately.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We set a high bar, move quickly and give people meaningful ownership. Support is a core part of the product experience, and we expect it to be technically credible, responsive and human.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll work closely with Engineering, Product, Transformation and Customer Success. Customer Success owns adoption and customer health; Transformation owns implementation; Account Management owns renewals and commercial growth; and Support Engineering owns technical investigation and resolution.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Wordsmith</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll support a fast-growing product used for important work inside some of the world’s most ambitious organisations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Because we’re building in a new technical category, the problems are interesting. You’ll work across software behaviour, integrations, data an