sis and commentary on the business of law and the strategy, performance and leadership of the world’s leading law firms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a growing, multi-site organisation, with colleagues working across research, data, technology, product, journalism, commercial and events in London, Leeds and Bristol.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior specialist role within our People &amp; Business Operations team. You will be the organisation's expert on employee relations, providing guidance and directly managing complex people matters, maintaining effective working relationships with union representatives, including regular engagement and the resolution of collective issues, supporting business change and ensuring our people frameworks remain effective, practical and legally compliant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alongside complex casework, you will take ownership of key people frameworks, ensuring decisions relating to progression, promotion and employee relations are applied consistently and fairly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role offers the opportunity to shape how Legal 500 approaches employee relations, people governance and organisational frameworks over the coming years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employee Relations &amp; Advice</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead on complex employee relations matters, providing expert advice and guidance to managers and senior stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the management of investigations, disciplinary, grievance, performance, capability and absence cases where senior specialist input is required</p></li><li><p style="min-he