nes how care is coordinated, purpose-built for the complexity of specialty pharmacy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building toward a world where pharmacy teams spend their time on patients, not paperwork - where AI handles the routine so clinicians can focus on what only humans can do. Getting there takes the right people. We're looking for curious, ambitious folks who want to help solve healthcare's hardest problems - for our patients, our partners, and each other.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team: AI-native by design</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our VP of Engineering comes from DeepMind/Google, and we're building with AI from day one, both in the product and in how we engineer. We use AI tools to move faster, automate repetitive work and spend more time on problems that need real engineering judgement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll actually be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing and building the back-end systems that connect pharmacies, health systems and insurers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solving hard distributed-systems problems: event-driven workflows, retries, idempotency, data consistency and failure recovery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning substantial features from the initial problem through architecture, build, deployment and production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Making pragmatic technical decisions as we scale, without overengineering for problems we don't have yet</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building AI-powered capabilities into a live product, where reliability and correctness matter as much as speed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working directly with product and engineering leadership to shape the roadmap, architecture and what we build next</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manchester: where our core engineering team works</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our core engineering team is based in Manchester city centre. We're in the office together 1–2 days a week to work through hard problems and debate technical decisions. The rest of the week, work wherever you're most effective.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not in Manchester yet? If you'd consider relocating, we can help with the move.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why you'd leave your current role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your work reaches real users</strong>. We're live with enterprise customers, so what you ship gets used, not lost in a backlog.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interesting engineering problems</strong>. We're connecting fragmented healthcare systems, where data integrity and correctness really matter. This isn't a CRUD app with an AI feature bolted on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real ownership</strong>. You'll shape solutions, challenge assumptions and influence the roadmap and architecture. We want you making important technical decisions, not just implementing someone else's.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>No legacy baggage</strong>. We're on a modern Node.js, TypeScript and GCP stack. You don't need to know it already. We care far more about the systems you've built than the tools you used.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity</strong>. You'll own a stake in the company you're helping build.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we do care about</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong engineering judgement</strong>. You can take an ambiguous problem, work out what matters, make sensible trade-offs and deliver without every step mapped out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Back-end depth</strong>. You've built and operated production systems and know what happens beyond the happy path: distributed systems, databases, performance, observability and failure recovery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership beyond the code</strong>. You think about how a feature behaves in production, how customers use it and what could go wrong. You've made technical decisions with real consequences and can explain why you made them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A builder's mindset</strong>. You've taken meaningful projects from idea to reality, at work or in your own time, and can explain the decisions and trade-offs you made.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curiosity about AI</strong>. You've built AI products, use AI to improve how you work, or are actively exploring what's possible. You don't need to be an ML researcher.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong fundamentals</strong>. You reason from first principles and pick up unfamiliar tech quickly. A degree in Computer Science, Maths, Physics or Engineering is useful, but depth of engineering ability matters most.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interested?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The funding's in place, the product is live and customers are asking for more than we can build. We're hiring engineers in Manchester to help close that gap.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/foundation-health/software-engineer-manchester-309875","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Manchester","created_at":1792680017},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-england-47647","company_name":"True Talent Solutions Partners","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","description":"<h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join a product engineering team building AI-powered software for certification, inspection, and compliance workflows. You will work closely with customers to understand real operational needs and turn them into reliable systems used in the field.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with customer operations teams to understand how certification, inspection, and compliance processes run in practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead customer calls, write specifications, and build end-to-end solutions across frontend, backend, data models, and AI components.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of product areas and collaborate directly with company leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship software quickly, observe how users work with it, and refine it based on feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use sound judgment to distinguish broadly useful product needs from customer-specific requests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review customer documents and outputs to develop AI-enabled workflows for scheduling, technical review, conformity assessment, field inspection, and document intelligence.</p></li></ul><h3>What We're Looking For</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Three to six years of experience in software or product engineering, with a record of shipping production systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full-stack development skills, including Python, TypeScript, React, Node.js, SQL, data modeling, and cloud infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building products or systems from the ground up, ideally in an early-stage or founding engineering role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with AI/ML, large language models, or document intelligence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence working directly with customers and translating operational workflows into software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience outside professional services or consulting environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Forward-deployed engineering experience is a plus.</p></li></ul><h3>Compensation &amp; Benefits</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salary range: £100,000 to £160,000 annually. Visa sponsorship is available.</p><h3>Location</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">On-site, five days per week in England, United Kingdom.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/true-talent-solutions-partners/forward-deployed-engineer-england-47647","tags":["Client Roles"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"England","created_at":1792680017},{"slug":"software-engineer-autonomous-agents-london-248722","company_name":"Kraken","title":"Software Engineer (Autonomous Agents)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Help us use technology to make a big green dent in the universe!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://kraken.tech/"><u>Kraken</u></a> powers some of the most innovative global developments in energy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the technology that redefines utilities and unlocks a new energy system of the future. By optimising renewable generation, building a more intelligent grid, and empowering utilities to deliver an exceptional customer experience, our operating system is transforming the industry worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s an incredibly exciting time to work in energy. Join us on our mission to improve the lives of ONE BILLION humans within the decade and shape a cleaner, better future for everyone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is a key investment area for Kraken Technologies. You’ll join <strong>Autonomous Agents</strong>, the team building AI-powered customer service for the energy industry. We connect conversational AI to Kraken’s customer platform so agents can do more than answer questions: they can use account information and approved tools to resolve real customer needs, like understanding a bill or submitting a meter reading, and hand over to a person, with full context, when it matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re launching autonomous agents with our utilities clients and the demand is growing quickly. The team is moving from initial trials to long-term production use, and we’re scaling from client-specific builds to a reusable product that can serve many clients. We’re growing the team to make that happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏡 Where you'll fit in:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll join a cross-functional team of around 10 engineers, alongside product and machine learning specialists, working closely with Kraken platform teams. The work spans two connected areas, and you’ll contribute to both:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build:</strong> the reusable core of the product. This covers client-agnostic agent journeys and tooling, MCP interfaces into Kraken, email, messaging and voice capabilities, and the observability, feature toggles and guardrails that let us roll out safely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Implementation:</strong> taking that core to individual clients. You’ll work with client teams to understand their customer journeys, configure and extend what we’ve built, and feed what you learn back into the shared product.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on engineering role. You’ll work alongside senior engineers and leads who will support your growth, while owning meaningful pieces of work from the first few months.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>👾 What you'll own:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Connect the dots:</strong> Investigate customer support queries, get to grips with regulatory and business processes, and turn them into clear technical plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring agents to life:</strong> Build integrations between Kraken, Model Context Protocol (MCP) interfaces and our AI agent setup, using Python on the Kraken side and TypeScript on the agent side.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build once, reuse everywhere:</strong> Spot patterns across customer journeys and client needs, and turn them into reusable, client-agnostic components rather than one-off fixes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make it safe and reliable:</strong> Build authentication, permissions, validation and human handoff into the design, and help us test and monitor behaviour that is less predictable than traditional software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Roll out with confidence:</strong> Ship features behind toggles, tested and documented, so they can be introduced gradually across clients and teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work with clients and teammates:</strong> Take part in client conversations, explain technical details clearly, document decisions and keep your commitments on track.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operate what you build:</strong> Contribute to dashboards, monitoring and runbooks so the services you ship are observable and supportable in production.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 What you bring to the party:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solid software engineering:</strong> You have shipped and supported production software, and you’re comfortable with testing, code review and working in a team codebase.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Python and TypeScript:</strong> You write clean, maintainable code in both and are happy moving between tools and environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Problem-first thinking:</strong> You take time to understand the problem before jumping to the first solution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Curiosity about AI:</strong> You’re interested in LLMs, autonomous agents and MCP, and in how to give agents the right context and tools. Hands-on experience is great, but you don’t need to have all the answers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer and client awareness:</strong> You’re comfortable talking to non-engineers, asking good questions and translating messy real-world processes into software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reliable delivery:</strong> You’re organised, write clear documentation and follow through on what you take on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning agility:</strong> You welcome feedback, ask questions when things are ambiguous and enjoy learning alongside others in a field that changes fast.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 What success looks like:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delivery:</strong> You ship well-scoped features and integrations that make it into production and are used by real clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reusability:</strong> Your work strengthens the shared product, so the next client is easier to onboard than the last.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Trust:</strong> Agents you help build behave safely, resolve customer needs correctly and hand over to people when they should.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth:</strong> You take on increasing ownership and become a go-to person for part of the platform.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">⭐️ <strong>Bonus points:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI engineering:</strong> Building with LLMs, agent frameworks or MCP servers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Conversational AI:</strong> Experience with customer service automation, voice or messaging channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Evals and monitoring:</strong> Testing, evaluating or monitoring non-deterministic systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Backend:</strong> Django</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Observability:</strong> Datadog, Sentry</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Client-facing experience:</strong> Working directly with customers or partners on technical delivery</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Are you ready for a career with us? We want to ensure you have the right tools and environment to unleash your potential. If you have any accommodation requests, please contact us at ----- We’ll do our best to tailor the experience to your needs so you can feel comfortable, confident and be at your best!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Studies have shown that some groups of people, like women, are less likely to apply to a role unless they meet 100% of the job requirements. Whoever you are, if you like one of our jobs, we encourage you to apply as you might just be the candidate we’re looking for! At Kraken, we're creating a team of genuine, honest, empathetic people. Our people are our strongest asset and the unique skills and perspectives people bring to the team are the driving force of our success. As an equal opportunity employer, we do not discriminate on the basis of any protected attribute. We consider all applicants without regard to race, colour, religion, national origin, age, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, marital or veteran status, disability, or any ot