 worth $250m to $1bn+ in total contract value, from selection through signature.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the commercial playbook: pricing structures, walk-away positions, a concession log, and fallback positions on liability, service levels, and exit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agree one position before you sit down. Rank priorities as must-have, trade, or give, and define your walk-away point (your best alternative to a negotiated agreement, or BATNA).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structure deals that fit the risk: fixed price, time and materials, outcome-based, and gain-share, with volume bands, rate cards, indexation, and price-down glide paths.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide which risks to transfer, share, or keep, and put a price on each one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate core billing and Customer Information System (CIS) replacements, including migration plans, regulatory change, service levels, and exit terms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define scope precisely: baseline, assumptions, dependencies, and exclusions. Most disputes start here, so you'll settle them before signature.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan the exit from day one: lock-in, data portability, step-in rights, and termination assistance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build competitive tension, keep alternatives alive, and manage timing, such as a vendor's quarter-end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring Delivery and Operations into the deal early, so the contract works in practice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lock in key-personnel clauses, so the vendor's A-team doesn't sell while the B-team delivers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up governance, benchmarking, and audit rights that keep working after signature, and track change requests, renewals, and exit costs alongside the headline price.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruit and grow 