em">Technical depth. You can challenge a vendor's assumptions on scope, effort, and architecture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scope and requirements clarity. You define what's in, what's out, and what has to be true for the price to hold.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exit and transition planning. You cover lock-in, data portability, step-in, and termination assistance from the start.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial modeling. You build multi-year margin, cash flow, cost-to-serve, and should-cost models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How you work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring one voice to the table. No side deals, and every concession goes in the log.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You build leverage with a competitive process, and you keep your composure when a vendor pushes a deadline or a "sign now for a discount" offer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You push hard on terms and protect the long-term partnership, because we'll live with the deal for years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work well across cultures and time zones, including with vendors based in other markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring legal, commercial, and technical colleagues into one room instead of letting them negotiate in silos.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>⭐ Bonus points</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time spent on the supplier side, so you know how vendor economics and margin levers work from the inside.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A legal or contracts background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiation or value-selling certifications, such as Harvard PON.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of Ofgem licence conditions, the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), and operational resilience rules such as the Digital Ope