rnal customer:</strong> deploy Kernel on Kernel’s CRM, use it to improve our GTM data and turn what we learn into useful feedback for Product and Engineering</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You Bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3+ years of experience</strong> in Revenue Operations or Sales Operations at a high-growth Series A-D SaaS company. You have owned meaningful parts of the revenue engine end to end, ideally as the first or one of the first RevOps operators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep Salesforce fluency:</strong> you understand objects, record types, fields, formulas, flows, validation rules, permissions, reports and data migration. You can reason about architecture and debug production behaviour</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial judgement:</strong> you understand how meetings become pipeline, how pipeline is qualified and forecast, and how won revenue flows into implementation, expansion, renewal and retention</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical building ability:</strong> you have built and deployed AI or agent-assisted workflows into real operating processes, are comfortable with connecting different systems together, and can debug how systems behave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong analytical skills:</strong> you can build funnel, capacity and revenue models, work confidently in spreadsheets, and reconcile numbers across systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Clear, low-ego communication:</strong> you can turn a messy request into a crisp decision, explain trade-offs to non-technical teams, push back constructively and drive adoption through influence rather than authority</p></li></ul><h3>It is a plus if you also have:</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience supporting an enterprise sales motion with multi-stakeholder deals and MEDDPICC.</p></li>