se en ligne des opérations commerciales spécifiques : ventes aux employés, ventes privées en ligne avec des prestataires</span></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">· Participation aux projets annexes inhérents à la roadmap E-merchandising</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p><span style="color:#121317">Etudiant en école de commerce ou de mode : </span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Vous démontrez un fort intérêt pour l’industrie de la mode, le luxe, et vous aimez les chiffres. </span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Doté.e d'un profil autonome, vous êtes reconnu.e pour votre rigueur, organisation et sens du détail.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">La connaissance de Shopify+, GA4 et des outils d’analyses est un plus pour ce poste ainsi qu'une maîtrise avancée d’Excel. </span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Langues : Anglais courant (indispensable) / Français courant</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><u><span style="color:#000000">Stage de 6 mois conventionné par un établissement reconnu par l’Etat uniquement, à pourvoir fin FEVRIER 2026</span></u></strong><span style="color:#000000">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em><span style="color:#121317">Nous sommes convaincus que la diversité de nos équipes est une force. Nous étudions toutes les candidatures avec la même attention, sans distinction de genre, de handicap, d'origine, d'âge ou d'orientation.</span></em></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/ami-paris/stage-e-merchandising-performance-assistant-h-f-paris-275869","tags":["Ecommerce"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Paris, Île-de-France, France","created_at":1792669905},{"slug":"remote-sales-account-executive-cybersecurity-montrouge-169464","company_name":"Crowdsec","title":"Sales Account Executive - Cybersecurity","description":"<p>Passionate about Cybersecurity, open-source or network effect products? Interested in Sales? </p><p>Join CrowdSec to build a safer internet for everyone.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.3em">What we do</span></strong></p><p>We aim to deter opportunistic and organized cybercrime through an Internet-scale, real-time security network. This network is powered by hundreds of thousands of servers sharing the aggression they block with our open-source software. By coupling this local behavior analysis and sharing its findings within our community, we create a real-time map of IP addresses used by cybercriminals, a large-scale reputation system, and a Crowd-Sourced Cyber Threat Intelligence of unprecedented magnitude that will counter the vast majority of technical hacks.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.3em">Who We Are</span></strong></p><p>CrowdSec is a human-sized team of cybersecurity experts. Most of the team has worked remotely since day 1. The CrowdSec solution is used in 180+ countries, it is a well-known, unique, collaborative, open-source security solution that protects hundreds thousands of users. We are animated by a mission: making the Internet a safer place, all together.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="font-size:1.3em">Role</span></strong></p><p>As an Account Executive (AE), you will work with the Sales team to help them scale, create new opportunities, interact with them, convert them to Leads, and take the accounts to signature. This will be done in collaboration with the BDRs, presales, Marketing, and Support teams to ensure the most pleasant customer journey.<br></p> <br> <p><strong>Must-have</strong></p><ul><li><p>A track record of success in selling Cybersecurity software solutions</p></li><li><p>A pre-existing customer/contact base to work on to kickstart your tenure</p></li><li><p>Knowledges of fundamental cybersecurity mechanism</p></li><li><p>Good methodology to deal with inbound leads</p></li><li><p>Good outreach techniques to convert SQLs to clients</p></li><li><p>Experience covering the whole sales process from prospection to signature</p></li><li><p>The ability to build relationships and credibility with both SOC Managers/analysts, DevOps, SecOps, Risk Managers, and C-level Executives alike</p></li><li><p>Predictability and accurate forecasting capabilities</p></li><li><p>Fluency in English and at least a second language; any supplementary languages are considered a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Optional</strong></p><ul><li><p>You have sold to SaaS, PaaS, IaaS, MSSPs or MSPs</p></li><li><p>Knowledge of the open-software landscape</p></li><li><p>Languages other than English and French&nbsp;are considered a plus</p></li><li><p>Start-up experience</p></li><li><p>Experience with Hubspot</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Soft Skills</strong></p><ul><li><p>You are a confident and polished communicator able to build&nbsp;strong and lasting relationships</p></li><li><p>You are autonomous, do not hesitate to share new ideas with the team, and are genuinely interested in learning your customer's needs</p></li><li><p>You are located in a&nbsp;+/- 6h from CEST Timezone</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Why join CrowdSec?</strong></p><ul><li><p>You want to take part in an adventure with a bleeding edge tech startup</p></li><li><p>Work with a team of blackbelt pros in their fields and interact with an exciting community</p></li><li><p>You are driven and energetic, with a passion for prospecting and driving pipeline</p></li><li><p>We are a full-remote company, we meet twice a year to strengthen the team spirit during a 1-week seminar.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/crowdsec/remote-sales-account-executive-cybersecurity-montrouge-169464","tags":["Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1792669904},{"slug":"ml-platform-engineer-paris-113846","company_name":"Bleu Robotics","title":"ML Platform Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>About us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bleu Robotics is an AI company developing universal AI software for the deployment of advanced robots , humanoids, mobile manipulators, and industrial arms, in real factories. The convergence of humanoid robotics and modern AI is one of the most significant technical opportunities of the decade, and most of the work today still happens in research settings. We are building the software layer required to bring it into operational use.<br /><br />We have a strong ambition to become the next Microsoft to run on every industrial humanoid.  We  have closed our pre-seed round with Top-tier fund to deploy our robot in Tier 1 manufacturing facilities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for deeply passionate scientists who can help us push the frontier and build a major lab in physical AI.<br /></p><h2><strong>Our vision</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>To enable a robot to learn a new industrial task from a few demonstrations and operate autonomously, with under one hour between the start of the demonstration and the start of deployment.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This objective shapes our roadmap and every technical decision we make.</p><h2><strong>THE ROLE</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hiring an ML Platform Engineer to put our robot learning stack in the cloud and own the full stack. The platform will let customers run our learning pipelines on their own data as a hosted service; its exact scope will evolve with the product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the first engineer at Bleu Robotics with cloud expertise. The scope covers infrastructure, training and inference services, the web front end, security, and cost. The choice of cloud provider and web framework is open; you will make it with the team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is based in Paris and is on-site. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>BACKGROUND</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are equally interested in two kinds of background:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">software or ML platform engineer who has built and operated a cloud service that runs training or inference jobs on data uploaded by users (e.g., an ML platform team, an MLOps product, a SaaS that runs compute on customer data).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">backend or full-stack engineer with solid DevOps experience who has shipped a web product on a major cloud provider and wants to work on robot learning.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with robotics or robot learning is appreciated but not required. You will learn the learning stack from the team; the team will learn cloud practices from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the architecture of the platform and select the cloud provider, orchestration layer, and web stack, in agreement with the team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Package our training and inference pipelines (Python, PyTorch) as cloud services: job scheduling, GPU provisioning, artifact storage, versioning of datasets and policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the web application through which users upload data, follow training runs, and download policies, including its front end and API</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Add interactive, browser-based components to the platform, including simulation, as the product evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up infrastructure as code, CI/CD, monitoring, logging, and alerting for the platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement authentication, per-customer isolation, and data protection for confidential industrial data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Control cloud costs: GPU usage, storage, and idle resources</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring cloud and DevOps practices to the rest of the engineering team through documentation, reviews, and training</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s degree or PhD in computer science or a related field, followed by 2 to 3 years of professional experience building and operating a comparable cloud service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience running production workloads on at least one major cloud provider (AWS, GCP, Azure, or a European provider such as Scaleway or OVHcloud)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency with containers and orchestration (Docker and Kubernetes or a managed equivalent) and with infrastructure as code (Terraform or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Python development skills for backend services, including asynchronous job execution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Front-end development experience with a modern web framework (React, Vue, Svelte, or similar), sufficient to ship the user-facing application yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CI/CD, monitoring, and security practices for a multi-tenant service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in Linux environments with Git</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional proficiency in English, the official language of the team. Proficiency in French is not required; many of our employees do not speak French.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The strongest candidates will combine cloud fluency with experience across several of the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ML infrastructure: training job orchestration, GPU scheduling, experiment tracking, model registries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PyTorch and the Python machine learning ecosystem</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physics simulation (MuJoCo, Isaac Sim, or similar) and 3D rendering in the browser (WebGL, three.js)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Streaming interactive content to the browser (WebRTC or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data engineering for large volumes of video and time-series data</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Security and compliance requirements of industrial customers: data residency, access control, audit logs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cost optimization of GPU workloads</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An early-stage startup, or a leading research lab (academic or industrial)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>THE TEAM</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The engineering team is a dozen top engineers and researchers in robotics and machine learning, organized around three focus areas: Integration, Vision &amp; Perception, and Robot Learning. This position is the first cloud and platform role at Bleu Robotics. You will work with the whole team and with the founders on product decisions. Early hires help shape engineering practices, hiring, and culture.<br /></p><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear, ambitious research mission with measurable real-world impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A diverse fleet of advanced robots, including humanoids, on which to run your research</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Research that ships: your algorithms run on real machines in real factories</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tight collaboration with engineering teams that take your work to production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant ownership of the research agenda as an early member of the team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A focused, technically strong team and a serious engineering culture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">English-speaking working environment, no French required</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fair compensation + equity </p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/bleu-robotics/ml-platform-engineer-paris-113846","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1792669233},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-paris-321286","company_name":"Linkup","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a <strong>top-tier Forward Deployed Engineer</strong> to join Linkup and work hand-in-hand with our founders, customers, and partners. You'll be part of the founding FDE team at Linkup </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mission: help leading AI companies, developers, and enterprises integrate Linkup’s AI-ready search APIs into their products - and shape how the next generation of AI agents connects to the web.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a highly cross-functional role. You’ll operate at the intersection of <strong>engineering, GTM, and customer success</strong>, turning technical integrations into insights that drive our product roadmap, marketing narratives, and outbound strategy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be the connective bridge between what customers build with Linkup and how we tell that story to the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work directly with customers and partners</strong> to design, prototype, and deploy integrations of Linkup’s APIs into real-world agentic systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Participate in pre-sales efforts</strong> - technical discovery, proof-of-concept design, demo environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborate cross-functionally</strong> with backend, ML, and product teams to ensure performance and reliability at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with the GTM Engineer and DevRel team</strong> to turn customer learnings into automation, tutorials, and playbooks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Identify and implement technical integrations</strong> with our other partners in the value chain (workflow orchestration, AI frameworks, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Translate complex technical concepts</strong> into clear explanations for both developers and business audiences.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why This Role Matters</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every integration you build helps define <strong>how AI systems connect to live, trusted information</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll operate on the frontier between customers and product - bringing the voice of the field into everything we build and say.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work will inform:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The <strong>stories we tell</strong> in marketing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The <strong>use cases we automate</strong> in our GTM systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The <strong>features we prioritize</strong> in our roadmap.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you love blending engineering with impact - building things users actually depend on: this role is for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You’re a Great Fit If You</strong>