<li>Contribute to the development and implementation of a comprehensive EMEA patient advocacy strategy aligned with corporate and regional objectives, starting in the SMA community and building the FSHD relationships.</li>
<li>Ensure patient and caregiver perspectives are appropriately incorporated throughout the product lifecycle, from clinical development through commercialization.</li>
<li>Identify emerging opportunities and risks within the advocacy and policy environment and provide strategic recommendations to leadership.</li>
<li>Foster a patient-centric culture throughout the organization.</li>

<div>Build Meaningful Community Partnerships</div>

<li>Establish and maintain authentic, trusted relationships with regional and national patient organizations, advocacy leaders, caregivers, and community stakeholders.</li>
<li>Serve as the primary company representative to patient advocacy organizations associated with direct-to-market counties throughout EMEA</li>
<li>Support development of and monitor execution against a patient advocacy group engagement playbook for partner market countries ensuring advocate engagement follows Scholar Rock standards</li>
<li>Identify, deliver, and participate in collaborative initiatives that support disease awareness, education, research, access, and policy priorities.</li>
<li>Build long-term collaboration based on transparency, trust, and shared goals.</li>

<div>Generate Patient Insights</div>

<li>&nbsp;Execute patient advisory boards, caregiver councils, listening sessions, and community engagement initiatives.</li>
<li>Collect and translate patient insights into actionable recommendations for internal teams.</li>
<li>Partner with Medical Affairs, Clinical Development, and Market Access to ensure the patient voice informs strategic decision-making.</li>
<li>Drive initiatives that better understand the patient and caregiver journey across EMEA markets.<br><br></li>
<br><strong>Corporate Communications Leadership</strong><br><div>Corporate Reputation &amp; Narrative</div>

<li>&nbsp;Develop and execute a comprehensive EMEA communications strategy that enhances company reputation and stakeholder trust.</li>
<li>Shape and implement compelling corporate narratives that articulate the company's mission, vision, scientific innovation, and commitment to patients.</li>
<li>Ensure consistency of messaging and brand positioning across all EMEA communications activities.</li>
<li>Support the development of disease area leadership and corporate positioning strategies.</li>

<div>Media &amp; External Communications</div>

<li>Manage regional media relations and proactive communications opportunities.</li>
<li>Draft and oversee press releases, corporate announcements, leadership messaging, Q&amp;A documents, and stakeholder communications aligned with relevant global advocacy and communications plans</li>
<li>Support major corporate and product milestones and drive the regional comunication plans of key milestones, including regulatory decisions, clinical data presentations, launch activities, and access achievements.</li>
<li>Develop digital communications strategies and manage relevant corporate channels aligned with Global Communications plans</li>
<li>Monitor emerging issues and develop proactive communications plans and response strategies.</li>

<div>Executive Communications &amp; Thought Leadership</div>

<li>Partner with senior leaders to enhance visibility and thought leadership within the rare disease community.</li>
<li>Develop executive presentations, conference materials, speeches, articles, and strategic messaging.</li>
<li>Support participation at patient, scientific, industry, and policy events across EMEA.</li>
<li>Position company leaders as credible and trusted voices within the neuromuscular disease ecosystem.</li>
<br><strong>Internal Communications</strong><br>
<li>Develop internal communication strategies that foster employee engagement and organizational alignment.</li>
<li>Support communications related to business updates, organizational initiatives, and company milestones.</li>
<li>Reinforce company culture and mission through effective storytelling and employee engagement programs.</li>
<li>Ensure employees remain connected to the needs and experiences of patients and caregivers.</li>
<br><strong>Cross-Functional Leadership</strong><br>
<li>Collaborate closely with Global Advocacy and Communications, Medical Affairs, Market Access, Commercial, Legal, Compliance, Regulatory Affairs, and Clinical Development Teams.</li>
<li>Act as a strategic partner across functions to align patient advocacy and communications initiatives with broader business priorities.</li>
<li>Ensure all activities comply with applicable regulations, industry codes, and company policies.</li>
<li>Provide patient engagement and communications expertise to internal stakeholders and project teams.</li>
<br><strong>Candidate Qualifications </strong><br><div>
<p><strong>Education</strong></p>
